.TH DWM 1 dwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwm \- dynamic window manager with the look and controls of i3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dwm is a dynamic window manager for X. This build keeps dwm's core and adds
the look and key bindings of an i3 session: per-window title bars, i3 colors,
tabbed and stacking layouts, binding modes for resizing and moving, a taskbar
and a system tray.
.P
Every client lives in a frame with an 18px title bar that shows its icon (its
.BR _NET_WM_ICON ,
or else the icon theme's icon for its class) and its title. The focused frame
gets a 2px orange outline, drawn by dwm itself on an input-transparent
overlay. Windows that draw their own decorations (no decorations in
.BR _MOTIF_WM_HINTS )
get no title bar, except as tiled windows of the tabbed layout. Windows with
a 32-bit (ARGB) visual get a frame of the same depth, so their transparency
works with a compositor.
.P
.B Tasks
group the workspaces: each task has its own tags 1..10, with their own
windows, layouts and factors, and remembers the viewed tags and the focused
window of every monitor. The tasks are shown left of the tags; the active one
is the same on every monitor. Tasks are created, renamed and removed at
runtime and their labels are kept in
.BR ~/.dwm/tasks .
New windows open in the active task.
.P
The layouts are:
.TP
.B splith ([]=)
master column on the left, stack on the right (the i3 default).
.TP
.B splitv ([v])
master row on top, stack below.
.TP
.B stacking ([S])
every tiled window fills the work area, overlapping.
.TP
.B tabbed ([T])
the title bar of the visible window becomes a shared tab strip with one tab
per tiled window; only the active tab is mapped.
.TP
.B floating (><>)
windows are placed and sized freely.
.P
Tiled windows are separated by 10px gaps, with the same gap at the monitor
edges. Windows that do not tile (floating rules, dialog, utility, splash,
toolbar and notification windows, transients, fixed-size windows such as
GCR/keyring prompts) open floating and centered on
their monitor, at most 1310x710 (i3's
.BR floating_maximum_size ).
.P
Windows are grouped by ten tags, the i3 workspaces 1 to 10, published as the
EWMH desktops (pagers and window switchers can read and change them). Each
tag remembers its own layout, master area size and number of master windows,
so changing them on one tag does not affect the others; when several tags are
viewed together, the first one provides them.
.P
The bar shows the tags (the selected one framed in orange, occupied ones
followed by a dot), the active binding mode, a taskbar with the windows of
the viewed tags (the focused one framed in orange), the status text read from
the root window name, and the system tray.
.SS Focus
Focus follows clicks, not the mouse: clicking a window, its title, its tab or
its taskbar entry focuses it.
A minimized window (dimmed in the taskbar) is hidden and left out of the
layout until its entry is clicked again or it is activated; it then comes
back exactly where it was, with the focus. When the focused window goes away, or when the
view changes to other tags, the keyboard goes to the most recently focused
window that is still visible.
.P
A
.B _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW
request (a client or a tool such as
.BR xdotool (1)
asking to activate a window) follows i3's
.BR "focus_on_window_activation smart" :
a window on a viewed tag is focused, a window on a hidden tag is marked
urgent instead. Tools that first switch to the window's desktop (such as
.B xdotool windowactivate
or window switchers) do get it focused. A
.B _NET_WM_STATE_DEMANDS_ATTENTION
request also marks a window urgent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH USAGE
.B Mod
is the Super (Mod4) key.
.SS Status bar
.TP
.B X root window name
is read and displayed in the status text area. It can be set with the
.BR xsetroot (1)
command;
.B dwm-clock
keeps it set to the date and time.
.TP
.B Button1
on a task label switches to that task.
.TP
.B Button3
on a task label renames that task.
.TP
.B Mod\-Button1
on a task label moves the focused window to that task.
.TP
.B Button1
on a tag label views that tag; on a taskbar entry focuses that window, or
minimizes it when it is already focused, or restores it when it is
minimized; on the status text opens the polybar calendar popup.
.TP
.B Mod\-Button2
on a taskbar entry swaps the focused window with the master (tiled layouts
only).
.SS Keyboard commands
.TP
.B Mod\-Return
Start
.BR st (1).
.TP
.B Mod\-d
Start
.BR launcher-rs .
.TP
.B Mod\-f
Start
.BR pcmanfm (1).
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-s
Start
.BR "flameshot gui" .
.TP
.B Mod\-q
Close the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod\-Left / Down / Up / Right
Focus the nearest window in that direction. In the tabbed and stacking
layouts Left/Right cycle through the tabs/windows instead, wrapping around.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-Left / Down / Up / Right
Move the focused window: a tiled window swaps places with its neighbour in
the tiling order, a floating window moves by 10px.
.TP
.B Mod\-h
Set the splith layout.
.TP
.B Mod\-v
Set the splitv layout.
.TP
.B Mod\-e
Toggle between splith and splitv.
.TP
.B Mod\-s
Set the stacking layout.
.TP
.B Mod\-w
Set the tabbed layout.
.TP
.B Mod\-space
Toggle the focused window between tiled and floating. A window that becomes
floating gets back the size and position it asked for when it was mapped.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-space
Move the focus between the tiled and the floating windows.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-f
Toggle fullscreen for the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod\-r
Enter (or leave) resize mode.
.TP
.B Mod\-m
Enter (or leave) move mode.
.TP
.B Mod\-[1..9], Mod\-0
View tag 1..9, or tag 10. Selecting the tag that is already viewed goes back
to the previous one (i3's
.BR workspace_auto_back_and_forth ,
.B autobackandforth
in config.h).
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-[1..9], Mod\-Shift\-0
Move the focused window to tag 1..9, or tag 10.
.TP
.B Mod\-Tab
View the previously selected tags (i3's
.BR back_and_forth ).
.TP
.B Mod\-Control\-[1..9], Mod\-Control\-0
Switch to task 1..9, or task 10. The active task again goes back to the
previous one.
.TP
.B Mod\-Alt\-Shift\-[1..9], Mod\-Alt\-Shift\-0
Move the focused window to task 1..10, keeping its tags.
.TP
.B Mod\-Prior / Mod\-Next
Switch to the previous/next task (Page Up/Down; wraps around).
.TP
.B Mod\-grave
Switch to the previously active task.
.TP
.B Mod\-n
Create a task after the active one, switch to it and edit its label in the
bar. It is named with the lowest free number until a label is typed.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-n
Edit the active task's label in the bar: type the label,
.B Return
keeps it,
.B Escape
cancels,
.B BackSpace
and
.B Control\-u
delete. An empty label keeps the old one.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-Delete
Remove the active task. Its windows move, with their tags, to the previous
task (the next one for the first task), which becomes active. The last task
is never removed.
.TP
.B Mod\-j / Mod\-k
Focus the next/previous window in the client list.
.TP
.B Mod\-b
Toggle the bar.
.TP
.B Mod\-, / Mod\-.
Focus the previous/next monitor, if any.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-, / Mod\-Shift\-.
Send the focused window to the previous/next monitor, if any.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-r, Mod\-Shift\-c
Restart dwm in place: dwm re-executes itself (picking up a newly installed
binary). Windows and the session helpers are kept, and so are each window's
tags, monitor, floating state and size factor, the window order, every tag's
layout and factors, the viewed tags and the focus.
.B dwm-restart
does the same from a shell.
.TP
.B Mod\-Shift\-e
Ask for confirmation with
.BR dwm-exit ,
then end the session.
.SS Binding modes
While a mode is active its name is shown in the bar and the keys below are
taken by dwm, so the focused window does not receive them.
.BR Return ,
.BR Escape ,
.B Mod\-r
or
.B Mod\-m
go back to normal mode.
.TP
.B Resize mode
Left/j and Right/; make the window narrower/wider, Up/l and Down/k make it
shorter/taller, like i3's resize mode. A floating window changes by 10px. For
a tiled window the direction that crosses the master/stack split moves the
split, and the other one changes the window's share of its column (splith)
or row (splitv), 2 percentage points per step. Shift\-Up/Shift\-Down
remove/add a master window.
.TP
.B Move mode
The arrows move a floating window by 10px (50px with Shift) or swap a tiled
window with its neighbour.
.SS Mouse commands
Any click on a window focuses it.
.TP
.B Button1
on the title bar of a floating window moves it while dragging; on a tab
focuses that tab.
.TP
.B Button2
on the title bar or the frame toggles between tiled and floating.
.TP
.B Button3
on the title bar or the frame resizes the window while dragging, from the
nearest edge or corner.
.TP
.B Mod\-Button1
anywhere on a window moves it while dragging. A tiled window stays tiled: when
released over another tiled window they swap places, over another monitor it
moves there.
.TP
.B Mod\-Button2
on the window toggles between tiled and floating.
.TP
.B Mod\-Button3
anywhere on a window resizes it while dragging. Tiled windows become
floating.
.P
Windows that draw their own title bar can also move and resize themselves
through
.BR _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
restart in place, like
.BR Mod\-Shift\-r .
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
quit cleanly: windows are handed back to the root window with their state
saved for the next window manager start.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.dwm/dwm-session
runs the autostart once and starts dwm again if it exits, until
.B ~/.dwm/exit
exists. A dwm that keeps exiting right after start is retried with a growing
delay.
.TP
.B ~/.dwm/dwm.log
dwm's error output for the current session (the previous one is kept as
.BR dwm.log.old ).
.TP
.BR dwm-restart ", " dwm-exit
signal the dwm of the current display (found through
.BR _NET_SUPPORTING_WM_CHECK " and " _NET_WM_PID
by
.BR dwm-wmpid ).
.TP
.B ~/.dwm/tasks
the task labels, one per line, rewritten on every change and read at start.
Without it the
.B deftasks
list of config.h is used.
.TP
.B ~/.dwm/autostart.sh
session helpers: tray applets, polkit agent, screen settings, the clock.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
dwm is customized by editing config.h and recompiling the source code.
.B make install
installs the binary and this page under ~/.local and the session files under
~/.dwm; a running dwm picks up the new binary on the next in-place restart.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR st (1),
.BR xsetroot (1),
.BR i3 (1)
.SH ISSUES
The icon theme lookup reads only PNG icons (the current GTK icon theme, the
themes it inherits, hicolor and pixmaps); SVG-only icons are not shown.
.SH BUGS
This is a personal build; report problems to its maintainer, not to
suckless.org.
